  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_horse_bell_cbefa58a0b79ec40addd2f1167f84b6f839e982fe436c5289756daba05b8bae798">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>(OED s.v. horse n. 27c) | small bells used for decoration on a horse’s trappings (OED s.v. bell n.1 1a) | a bell to hang around the neck of a horse (OED s.v. horse n. IV 27c), jingle bells (quote) Whanne he rood men myghte his brydel heere Gynglen in a whistlynge wynd as cleere And eek as loude as dooth the chapel belle (MED s.v. ginglen, quote from Chaucer 1387-95) | a bell to hang around the neck of a horse (OED s.v. horse n. 27c), jingle bells (quote) Whanne he rood men myghte his brydel heere Gynglen in a whistlynge wynd as cleere And eek as loude as dooth the chapel belle (MED s.v. ginglen, quote from Chaucer 1387-95)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
